1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,750
JustEnough — a Midnight DApp that proves eligibility instead of handing over documents.

2
00:00:05,652 --> 00:00:18,082
The institution needs three yes/no answers — residence, employment, income — but receives three whole documents. Most applicants are not selected, yet their papers stay behind.

3
00:00:18,986 --> 00:00:29,146
We keep the check and remove the documents: the issuer publishes one hash, the applicant submits one proof, the operator draws anonymous receipts.

4
00:00:30,047 --> 00:00:40,677
Midnight's dual ledger does the split: values and secrets stay on the applicant's device; the ledger holds hashes, the public rule and receipts.

5
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:47,860
The live demo. This page runs the compiled Compact circuits right in the browser — no wallet needed.

6
00:00:48,762 --> 00:00:56,862
The issuer issues applicant A's credential: one hash on the public ledger, the values only on A's device.

7
00:00:57,764 --> 00:01:05,804
The programme rule is public text anyway, so it goes on the ledger as is. Seven real notices were translated the same way.

8
00:01:06,705 --> 00:01:10,195
A checks all seven conditions on their own device,

9
00:01:11,096 --> 00:01:23,906
and applies with a single proof. Zero personal fields reach the institution. The "What the chain sees" panel shows one receipt hash, and a live re-scan of the public data finds none of A's private values.

10
00:01:24,809 --> 00:01:29,599
Applying twice produces the same receipt, so the circuit refuses.

11
00:01:30,502 --> 00:01:35,172
B is employed. If B submits anyway, no proof can be produced.

12
00:01:36,072 --> 00:01:41,982
Rewriting the value to 'unemployed' fails too: the hash no longer matches anything the issuer published.

13
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:58,300
At closing the operator reveals the draw seed it committed before anyone applied. The 5 lowest tickets of 21 receipts win, anyone can recompute it, and the operator still doesn't know who is who.

14
00:01:59,201 --> 00:02:06,641
Only A, who was selected, proves the receipt is theirs and claims. Rejected applicants' data never reached the institution.

15
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:19,440
The same flow ran on a local Midnight network with real proofs: eight transactions, the seed matched its commitment, zero attribute values in the indexer's public state.

16
00:02:20,342 --> 00:02:25,052
Seven cheating attempts, all refused by the circuit and pinned by tests.

17
00:02:25,953 --> 00:02:34,873
118 tests, a 2,000-case differential test, compilation on two compiler versions, and the real-network run — all wired into CI.

18
00:02:35,776 --> 00:02:42,656
Clone once, run two commands, see for yourself. JustEnough — prove only what is needed.
